Subject: [PATCH] Exynos8895: retain UFS controller clocks after Hibern8

The Samsung sequence does not stop the UFS controller clocks after
Hibern8 entry. Keep them accessible on Exynos8895 while the UFS core
stops the host and runs normal shutdown. The PHY and clock teardown
steps still run through the suspend paths.

Depends on the Exynos8895 UniPro Hibern8 completion proposal.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -1629,6 +1629,14 @@
 
 	if (cmd == UIC_CMD_DME_HIBER_ENTER) {
 		ufs->entry_hibern8_t = ktime_get();
+		/*
+		 * The Exynos8895 vendor path leaves the clocks available
+		 * after Hibern8 so the core can still stop the controller.
+		 * Clock and PHY teardown remains in the suspend path.
+		 */
+		if (ufs->drv_data->native_hibern8_status)
+			return;
+
 		exynos_ufs_gate_clks(ufs);
 		if (ufs->opts & EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_BROKEN_AUTO_CLK_CTRL)
 			exynos_ufs_enable_auto_ctrl_hcc(ufs);
